From cf34743ea00cdcb7aeadd42074c5383c3a4480a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fei Yunbin <realshadow4869@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 14:03:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] OfficeViewer: preview performance optimization +
 Protected View copy-preview

Performance (O1-O4):
- New OfficePreviewHostPool.cs: keeps the Office IClassFactory alive for ~2ms warm
  activation, and adds an idle watchdog that calls LockServer(false) + releases the
  factory on the UI thread so the Office processes actually exit (fixes the 355MB
  permanently-resident WINWORD/EXCEL/POWERPNT leak).
- Drop the blocking GC.Collect() from PreviewHandlerHost.Dispose() - it ran on the WPF
  UI thread on every preview close.
- Remember which IInitialize* flavour actually succeeded per CLSID instead of probing
  IInitializeWithStream -> WithItem -> WithFile on every preview (Office handlers only
  implement IInitializeWithFile).
- Two-stage background warm-up (WarmUpAfterFirstPreview default on, WarmUpAtStartup
  default off) so the 480-860ms cold activation moves off the user-visible path.
- Log per-preview timing.

Protected View:
- Never touch the user's original file. When the document carries a Zone.Identifier,
  the plugin now renders an unblocked *copy* in %TEMP% and shows an amber banner
  saying so.
- The banner carries a button that unblocks the original file only when the user
  clicks it, after which the strip turns green.
- The blocking Yes/No confirmation dialog is removed entirely.

Build note: WindowInteropHelperExtension.cs is rewritten from the C#14 extension-block
syntax into an equivalent classic extension method so it compiles on .NET SDK 9.
