Subject: [PATCH 2/2] OfficeViewer: bilingual (zh/en) UI text for the Protected
 View notice

The notice strip, its button and the viewer title prefix were Chinese-only.
They now live in one place, UiText.cs, with a Chinese and an English variant.

The language follows the Windows UI language (CultureInfo.CurrentUICulture),
so nothing has to be configured; a new 'UiLanguage' setting (auto/zh/en) can
force one. Everything else QuickLook draws is untouched.

No behaviour change: same copy-preview path, same banner geometry, same
button semantics - only the strings moved.
